coder › Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts` and added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `src/toc.ts`: parses the markdown line by line, tracking ` ``` `-fenced code blocks (any line whose left-trimmed text starts with ` ``` `, including info strings like ` ```js `, toggles in/out). Outside fences, a line matching 1–6 `#` followed by a space is a heading; `level` is the hash count, `text` is the remainder trimmed. Slugs lowercase the text, replace each run of non-letter/digit characters with one dash, and trim leading/trailing dashes; repeats get `-2`, `-3`, … appended.
- `src/toc.test.ts` (new): 11 tests covering levels 1–6, missing-space rejection (`#Nope`), 7+ hashes ignored, text trimming, slug collapsing/trimming, duplicate `-2`/`-3` suffixes, slug-based (not text-based) dedup, fenced blocks skipped, fences with info strings, and empty/non-heading input.

