Decisions the task did not spell out:
- Fence detection is any line left-trimmed starting with ` ``` ` (info strings count); the fence lines themselves are never headings.
- Heading lines allow up to 3 leading spaces; 7+ `#` never match (regex backtracking can't turn the 7th `#` into the required space).
- "Letters or digits" uses Unicode properties (`\p{L}\p{N}`), so accented/non-Latin letters survive in slugs.
- Dedup guard: if a natural slug collides with an already-issued suffixed slug (e.g. headings `a`, `a`, `a-2`), the later one gets a further suffix (`a-2-2`), since that slug "has already been used".

